WEBVTT

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:25.018
Why? Somehow you seem upset
Why? Nandaka ochikonderu mitai

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:33.361
Voice, my voice. I want it to reach you
Voice, my voice. Todoketai yo kimi ni

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:41.840
Things aren't going the way you'd like
Omoi douri ni naranai koto nara

00:00:42.342 --> 00:00:50.342
That might happen a lot now, but...
Ima wa takusan attarisuru kedo

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:57.213
Tomorrow, another new wind
Mata ashita wa chigau kaze

00:00:57.624 --> 00:01:00.753
will blow your way
fuite kuru yo

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:05.760
Spread your arms and let your chest
Ryoute wo hirogeta mune ni

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:09.025
just feel the breeze
kanjiru mama

00:01:09.369 --> 00:01:13.931
No matter what befalls us,
Nani ga osoi kakattemo

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.266
no matter how difficult it may be
semetatete mo

00:01:18.011 --> 00:01:24.610
We'll be all right
Watashi tachi wa daijoubu

00:01:36.729 --> 00:01:37.457
Autumn.

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:44.098
They say leaves fall from the
branches to give way to new leaves.

00:01:45.538 --> 00:01:48.337
No matter how lonesome you feel
seeing the leaves fall...

00:01:49.275 --> 00:01:52.802
...hew leaves will return in the spring.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:04.178
Perhaps the emptiness left in your
heart is similar to the falling leaves.

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:15.626
The Category of Happiness

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:19.348
What? Ueno moved?

00:02:19.372 --> 00:02:22.451
Yeah, his father got transferred, so...

00:02:22.475 --> 00:02:23.486
...he's going to Hokkaido.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:26.241
So, it's a long distance
relationship? It must be lonely.

00:02:26.446 --> 00:02:29.058
But you know... the more obstacles,

00:02:29.082 --> 00:02:31.779
the more passionate love gets!

00:02:32.152 --> 00:02:33.210
You think so?

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:35.552
You're such a positive thinker, AKi.

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:39.424
Haven't you ever heard the proverb,
"Life is short, maidens be in love"?

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:41.221
That's not a proverb...

00:02:43.796 --> 00:02:45.594
Hey, Makoto! Let's go home!

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:47.593
Hold on.

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:51.097
I'm almost done inputting all the data.

00:02:51.304 --> 00:02:52.465
What are you doing?

00:02:53.406 --> 00:02:55.898
| finally got it yesterday!

00:02:56.142 --> 00:02:58.087
It's the secret weapon I've been waiting for!

00:02:58.111 --> 00:02:59.169
Secret weapon?
Secret weapon?

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:02.379
Listen and be amazed...

00:03:02.448 --> 00:03:05.227
It's the red string of destiny,
spun by the wisdom of mankind!

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:07.096
It's Dr. Kirara Mitsuboshi's supervised...

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:07.563
